    }","notes":"entrypoint_5 (mint 0x40c10f19) currently reverts because the body only guards and then falls through to a bare revert; the reference shows the same call succeeding (ok=true, no revert data) with owner set in setup step 0 and totalSupply 100e18 later readable, so the function must be a state-changing mint: keep the owner check (CustomError_30cd7471) and zero-address check (CustomError_d92e233d), then write the balance via the declared public balance mapping unresolved_70a08231 and emit the Transfer event Event_ddf252ad from address(0), matching the standard mint pattern implied by the later balance/supply reads. Also dropped the erroneous `view` qualifier since the reference call mutates storage (balance of the minted account and total supply are observed nonzero in subsequent reads) and a view function could not produce those effects."}
